<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila call loan rate falls as reserve needs met.</title>
<headline>Manila call loan rate falls as reserve needs met.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>-------------------------- Oct 4 -------------------------</p>
<p>* Liquidity seen boosted further on Monday</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Manila's interbank call loan average rate fell on Friday as most banks had met their reserve needs for the week, traders said.</p>
<p>The call rate average was down to 11.84375 percent from Thursday's 12.3125. Deals ranged between a high of 12.75 and a low of 11.25 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;On Monday, there's expectation of more money because of a 4.0 billion peso maturity,&quot; one trader said.</p>
</text>
